<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib69.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">arXiv preprint arXiv:2309.15818</em><span id="bib.bib69.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, 2023.
</span>
</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib70" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem"><span id="bib.bib70.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[70]</span></span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span id="bib.bib70.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Jason Zhang, Gengshan Yang, Shubham Tulsiani, and Deva Ramanan.
</span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span id="bib.bib70.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ners: Neural reflectance surfaces for sparse-view 3d reconstruction in the wild.
</span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib70.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems</em><span id="bib.bib70.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, 34:29835–29847, 2021.
</span>
</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib71" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem"><span id="bib.bib71.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[71]</span></span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span id="bib.bib71.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Richard Zhang, Phillip Isola, Alexei A Efros, Eli Shechtman, and Oliver Wang.
</span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span id="bib.bib71.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The unreasonable effectiveness of deep features as a perceptual metric.
</span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span id="bib.bib71.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">In </span><em id="bib.bib71.10" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">CVPR</em><span id="bib.bib71.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, 2018.
</span>
</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib72" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem"><span id="bib.bib72.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[72]</span></span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span id="bib.bib72.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Daquan Zhou, Weimin Wang, Hanshu Yan, Weiwei Lv, Yizhe Zhu, and Jiashi Feng.
</span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span id="bib.bib72.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Magicvideo: Efficient video generation with latent diffusion models.
</span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib72.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">arXiv preprint arXiv:2211.11018</em><span id="bib.bib72.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, 2022.
</span>
</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<br class="ltx_break ltx_centering">
</div>
<div id="p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:144%;">Supplementary Material 
<br class="ltx_break"></span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.01669v1/turn_i2v.png" id="S6.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/300;" width="685" height="300" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="S6.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The flowchart of how we transform a set of multi-view images into a initial video. Here we take an example with 5 input images and their poses. Given 5 unordered poses shown in (a), we firstly random choose a pose to initiate a double link list in (b). Next, we iteratively add the nearest pose to the list until all poses are in the list, shown in (c)(d)(e). Then in (f) we start from the head of the list and traverse the whole list and obtain the ordered poses in (g). Finally we add new poses to the intervals of input poses, making the trajectory dense and thus transform images to video.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>More Details for Method</h2>

<section id="S7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.1 </span>Sorting Images for Sparse Trajectory.</h3>

<div id="S7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Starting with <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> poses <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, we initialize a double linked list <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P^{l}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P^{l}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> with a randomly chosen pose <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{init}}\in\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>init</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{init}}\in\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is the length of the list.
At each iteration, for any pose <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{c}\in\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}\setminus\{P^{l}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{c}\in\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}\setminus\{P^{l}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, we calculate its distance with the list <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{PL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{PL}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="S7.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{PL}(P_{c},\{P^{l}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{L})=\min\{D_{P}(P_{c},P^{l}_{head}),D_{P}(P_{c},P^{l}_{tail})\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{PL}(P_{c},\{P^{l}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{L})=\min\{D_{P}(P_{c},P^{l}_{head}),D_{P}(P_{c},P^{l}_{tail})\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{l}_{head}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{l}_{head}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{l}_{tail}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{l}_{tail}</annotation></semantics></math> are the head and tail of the current list, i.e., <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{l}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{l}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{l}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{l}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. The distance between poses <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="S7.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{P}(P_{a},P_{b})=\frac{\omega_{r}}{s_{R}}\cdot D_{R}(R_{a},R_{b})+\frac{1-\omega_{r}}{s_{T}}\cdot D_{T}(T_{a},T_{b})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{P}(P_{a},P_{b})=\frac{\omega_{r}}{s_{R}}\cdot D_{R}(R_{a},R_{b})+\frac{1-\omega_{r}}{s_{T}}\cdot D_{T}(T_{a},T_{b}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> are the rotation matrix and translation vector of the pose <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is the weight for rotation distance, and <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> are scale factors to ensure rotation and translation distances have the same scale. We calculate the rotation distance <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="S7.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{R}(R_{a},R_{b})=\arccos\left(\frac{\text{trace}(R_{a}R_{b})-1}{2}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arccos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mtext>trace</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{R}(R_{a},R_{b})=\arccos\left(\frac{\text{trace}(R_{a}R_{b})-1}{2}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and the translation distance <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="S7.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{T}(T_{a},T_{b})=\|T_{a}-T_{b}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{T}(T_{a},T_{b})=\|T_{a}-T_{b}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">After calculating the distances of all <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P^{l}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P^{l}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, we add the new pose <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{new}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{new}</annotation></semantics></math> with minimal distance to the list:</p>
<table id="S7.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{new}=\mathop{\arg\min}_{P_{c}\in\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}\setminus\{P^{l}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{L}}D_{PL}(P_{new},\{P^{l}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{L})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{new}=\mathop{\arg\min}_{P_{c}\in\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}\setminus\{P^{l}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{L}}D_{PL}(P_{new},\{P^{l}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{L}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{new}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{new}</annotation></semantics></math> is closer to <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{l}_{head}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{l}_{head}</annotation></semantics></math>, we add an edge from <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{l}_{head}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{l}_{head}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{new}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{new}</annotation></semantics></math> and turn <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{new}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{new}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{l}_{head}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{l}_{head}</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise, we do the same for <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{l}_{tail}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{l}_{tail}</annotation></semantics></math>. We iteratively perform this process until all poses in <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> are added to the list. After that, we start from <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{head}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{head}</annotation></semantics></math> and traverse the whole list by edges to get an ordered set of poses <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P^{l}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P^{l}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">According to <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the ordered images <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{I^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{I^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. Along the ordered poses <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}_{1},P^{\prime}_{2},\ldots,P^{\prime}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}_{1},P^{\prime}_{2},\ldots,P^{\prime}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, we actually obtain an appropriate implicit camera trajectory. We show this process in both Alg. <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 7.1 Sorting Images for Sparse Trajectory. ‣ 7 More Details for Method ‣ UniVerse: Unleashing the Scene Prior of Video Diffusion Models forRobust Radiance Field Reconstruction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Fig. <a href="#S6.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ UniVerse: Unleashing the Scene Prior of Video Diffusion Models forRobust Radiance Field Reconstruction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> UniVerse</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="alg1.4" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom"><span id="alg1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Inconsistent multi-view images <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{I_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{I_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, rough camera poses <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, camera pose estimation method <math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Camera(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Camera(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> conditional video diffusion model <math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, number of images per iteration <math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, pose sort function <math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ThreadPose(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ThreadPose(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, the function to turn images to initial videos <math id="alg1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I2V(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I2V(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, transient occlusions segment model <math id="alg1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Seg(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Seg(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, 3D Reconstruction Method <math id="alg1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Recon(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Recon(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math></p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="alg1.5" class="ltx_listing ltx_figure_panel ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialization:</span> <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I^{re}{{}^{\prime}}\leftarrow\{\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msup><mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{re}{{}^{\prime}}\leftarrow\{\}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{I^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K},\{P^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{I^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K},\{P^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ThreadPose(\{I_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K},\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ThreadPose(\{I_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K},\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K})</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{sty}\leftarrow\text{manually/random choose an image from $\{I^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}$}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>manually/random choose an image from </mtext><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{sty}\leftarrow\text{manually/random choose an image from $\{I^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}$}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
              Initiate inpainting and style masks <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{in}\leftarrow\{\},M^{st}\leftarrow\{\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{in}\leftarrow\{\},M^{st}\leftarrow\{\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
              Extract the first <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> images: <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{I^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{I^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
