<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> Ordered poses <math id="alg2.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.2 </span>Sampling Implicit Views</h3>

<div id="S7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At each iteration, given <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> ordered poses <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and corresponding <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> inconsistent images <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{I^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{I^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, our goal now is to create a initial video of <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> frames inluding all the input <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> images. And we inflate it to <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> frames by sampling <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f-N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f-N</annotation></semantics></math> new poses and thus new views. First, we compute the distances <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{d_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{d_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N-1}</annotation></semantics></math> between neighboring poses:</p>
<table id="S7.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{i}=D_{P}(P^{\prime}_{i},P^{\prime}_{i+1}),\quad i=1,2,\ldots,N-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}=D_{P}(P^{\prime}_{i},P^{\prime}_{i+1}),\quad i=1,2,\ldots,N-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we determine the number of new poses <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to be inserted between each pair of neighboring poses <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, proportional to the distance <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S7.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="n_{i}=\left\lfloor\frac{d_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}d_{i}}\times(f-N)\right\rfloor,\quad i=1,2,\ldots,N-1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}=\left\lfloor\frac{d_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}d_{i}}\times(f-N)\right\rfloor,\quad i=1,2,\ldots,N-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lfloor x\right\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lfloor x\right\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the floor function, which gives the greatest integer <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq x</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the sum of <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> might not exactly equal <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f-N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f-N</annotation></semantics></math> due to the floor operation, we distribute the remaining poses. We calculate the remaining number of poses <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S7.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=(f-N)-\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}n_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=(f-N)-\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}n_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Then, we add one additional pose to the <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> largest intervals (i.e., the intervals with the largest <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> values) by incrementing <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for the <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> largest <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> values:</p>
<table id="S7.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}=n_{i}+\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }d_{i}\text{ is among the }r\text{ largest values},\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is among the </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> largest values</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}=n_{i}+\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }d_{i}\text{ is among the }r\text{ largest values},\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In this way, we obtain the number of inserted views. By inserting <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> zero frames into neighboring images <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{i}^{\prime},I^{\prime}_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{i}^{\prime},I^{\prime}_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get the initial video.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8 </span>More Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Adapt Video Diffusion Models with Mask Input:</h4>

<div id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We fine-tune the Video Diffusion Model from the <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="576\times 1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>576</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">576\times 1024</annotation></semantics></math> interpolation model of ViewCrafter <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>]</cite>. Since our method utilizes additional masks (<em id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e</em>.<span id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span> inpainting masks and style masks), we need to change the input dimension of the Denoising U-Net. We follow the fine-tuning approach of Inpainting Latent Diffusion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>. Specifically, we change an <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\times C\times\textit{kernel\_size}\times\textit{kernel\_size}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">kernel_size</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">kernel_size</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\times C\times\textit{kernel\_size}\times\textit{kernel\_size}</annotation></semantics></math> 2D convolutional kernel to <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\times C\times\textit{kernel\_size}\times\textit{kernel\_size}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">kernel_size</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">kernel_size</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\times C\times\textit{kernel\_size}\times\textit{kernel\_size}</annotation></semantics></math> by concatenating two additional masks. To do this, we maintain the original <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\times C\times\textit{kernel\_size}\times\textit{kernel\_size}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">kernel_size</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">kernel_size</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\times C\times\textit{kernel\_size}\times\textit{kernel\_size}</annotation></semantics></math> kernels and add zero-initialized <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times C\times\textit{kernel\_size}\times\textit{kernel\_size}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">kernel_size</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">kernel_size</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times C\times\textit{kernel\_size}\times\textit{kernel\_size}</annotation></semantics></math> kernels to it.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Detect All Transient Objects in Input Images:</h4>

<div id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the UniVerse pipeline, it is important to identify all transient objects to mask them. To achieve this, we first pre-define a set of transient prompts, such as <span id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[person, car, bike]</span>. We then use a Semantic Segmentation Model to detect the pixels of the objects in the prompts. Using the positions of these pixels, we employ the Segment Anything Model (SAM) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite> to precisely segment the objects and obtain the inpainting masks.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S9" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">9 </span>More Visual Results</h2>

<div id="S9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since UniVerse utilizes a VDM to turn initial videos into restored videos, we present several examples in Figs. <a href="#S9.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ 9 More Visual Results ‣ UniVerse: Unleashing the Scene Prior of Video Diffusion Models forRobust Radiance Field Reconstruction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, <a href="#S9.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ 9 More Visual Results ‣ UniVerse: Unleashing the Scene Prior of Video Diffusion Models forRobust Radiance Field Reconstruction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, and <a href="#S9.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ 9 More Visual Results ‣ UniVerse: Unleashing the Scene Prior of Video Diffusion Models forRobust Radiance Field Reconstruction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, demonstrating how UniVerse leverages the video prior to transform multi-view images into a consistent video. In these figures, the top row shows the initial video frames, while the bottom row displays the corresponding restored video frames. The frames are arranged from left to right in sequential order, with the first row showing frames 1-5, the second row showing frames 6-10, and so on.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S9.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.01669v1/app_video_horn.png" id="S9.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:651/884;" width="651" height="884" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S9.F11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="S9.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Visualization of how UniVerse turns a initial video into restored video.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S9.F12" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.01669v1/app_video_fern.png" id="S9.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:651/885;" width="651" height="885" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S9.F12.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12</span>: </span><span id="S9.F12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Visualization of how UniVerse turns a initial video into restored video.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
